#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# parametric_convex_optimization

#% text
# `parametric_convex_optimization(f, cons, vars, params)` gives a function of the parameters `params` that returns the minimizer of the convex problem for given parameter values.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `parametric_convex_optimization(f, cons, vars, params, prop)` returns the property `prop` ("PrimalMinimumValue", "PrimalMinimizer" or "PrimalMinimizerRules") instead of the rules.

#% item
# The parameters are a symbol or a list of up to three symbols; the returned function takes one value for each.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
parametric_convex_optimization(x + y, [x + y >= 3 + a, x >= -1], [x, y], a)(1)
#% output
#= [x -> -1, y -> 5]

#% cell
parametric_convex_optimization((x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2, [x >= 0, y >= 0, x + 2*y <= 1], [x, y], [a, b], "PrimalMinimumValue")(1, 1)
#% output
#= 4/5

#% cell
parametric_convex_optimization((x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2, [x >= 0, y >= 0, x + 2*y <= 1], [x, y], [a, b], "PrimalMinimumValue")(0, 0)
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `robust_convex_optimization`, `convex_optimization`, `minimize`
